00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:49.680
<v Clayton Gentry>So we would pick up these very specific patterns that could help us design our more automated systems later on.

239
00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:54.580
<v Clayton Gentry>So I think the lesson from doing that was when you immediately jump to scale,

240
00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:59.180
<v Clayton Gentry>the first mistake you might be making is you might be scaling something that shouldn't exist in the first place,

241
00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:06.000
<v Clayton Gentry>but also you might miss nuances that would have otherwise enriched your scaling efforts

242
00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:11.000
<v Clayton Gentry>had you implemented the process in a little bit more do-it-yourself fashion at the outset.

243
00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:14.140
<v Clayton Gentry>So that's what we learned from that content matching exercise.

